In Dragon Ball, Ki (also spelled chi or qi) is the tangible, vital life-force energy that exists inside every living being. It serves as the core power system of the franchise, allowing characters to perform superhuman feats through training and willpower.
According to the Dragon Ball Wiki, Ki is made up of three fundamental components:
• Genki (Vigor): Physical energy, health, and life force (used to power techniques like the Spirit Bomb / Genki Dama).
• Yūki (Courage): Emotional energy and drive; intense emotions like rage can break limits, while calm focus yields maximum efficiency.
• Shōki (Right-mindedness): Mental clarity, focus, and intent.

What Ki Can Do

• Physical Enhancement: Dramatically increases strength, speed, and durability by acting as an invisible protective energy shield.
• Energy Attacks: Projects destructive blasts, beams, and discs (such as the Kamehameha).
• Special Techniques: Enables flight, telekinesis, telepathy, and instantaneous movement via signature tracking (Instant Transmission).
• Sensing & Suppression: Allows skilled fighters to read and locate the energy signatures of others or mask their own to hide their power level.

Main Types of Ki

• Normal / Good Ki: Standard energy emitted by regular or positive-minded individuals, usually glowing white, yellow, or clear.
• Evil Ki: Corruptive energy born from dark, villainous, or malicious intent, often felt as cold or overwhelming (red or purple auras).
• Godly Ki (Divine Ki): A higher, more refined, and dense celestial energy utilized by deities and advanced transformations (such as Super Saiyan God) that regular mortals cannot easily sense unless they possess it themselves
